839	        // Replacing the log must work on Windows: ftruncate() of an open
840	        // append handle does not shrink the file there. Close the handle,
841	        // write a fresh marker-only log to a temp name, fsync it, then
842	        // atomically rename it over the old one (libuv replaces the target)
843	        // and reopen. The whole swap is one synchronous segment, so no
844	        // reader can observe an intermediate state.
845	        closeSync(fd);
